⍝ Print the report for one observation, as the book or modern version prints it
⍝ Used by Starmap/Tests/TestReport to capture printed output
⍝
⍝   REPORT_VERSION=book REPORT_PW=80 REPORT_OBS='5 16 1974 5 33.767 ¯117.833' \
⍝       dyalog -script test/report.apls
⍝
⍝ REPORT_VERSION is book or modern; REPORT_PW sets ⎕PW;
⍝ REPORT_OBS is month day year hour latitude longitude.
⍝ book:   sets the inputs as EXAMPLE_RENDER does, then runs WORK
⍝ modern: prints each line of (⎕PW ⎕TS)Work SkyAt, as Display does

⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
Env←{2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment'⍵}
'#.sm'⎕NS''
{2 #.sm.⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨⊃⎕NINFO⍠1⊢'APLSource/*.aplf'
{⍎'#.sm.',(2⊃⎕NPARTS ⍵),'←',∊(⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1),¨' '}¨⊃⎕NINFO⍠1⊢'APLSource/*.apla'
'#.Starmap'⎕NS''
{2 #.Starmap.⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨⊃⎕NINFO⍠1⊢'Starmap/*.aplf'
#.Starmap.Data←#.sm
⎕PW←⍎Env'REPORT_PW'
#.sm.OBS←⍎Env'REPORT_OBS'

∇ Book
  #.sm⍎'STATEDDAYNO←JNU 3↑OBS'
  #.sm⍎'STATEDTIME LAT LONG←3↓OBS'
  #.sm⍎'TIME←LONG TIMEADJUST STATEDTIME'
  #.sm⍎'DATE←STATEDDAYNO+(TIME÷24)-LONG÷360'
  #.sm.WORK
∇

∇ Modern;sky
  sky←#.Starmap.SkyAt(#.Starmap.JNU 3↑#.sm.OBS),3↓#.sm.OBS
  {⎕←⍵}¨(⎕PW ⎕TS)#.Starmap.Work sky
∇

⍎('book' 'modern'⍳⊂Env'REPORT_VERSION')⊃'Book' 'Modern'
⎕OFF
